description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, add a PREMISE CHECK that warns the drafter when a gap names a path that does not exist in the file it points at.

WHY, MEASURED. One gap asserts that GET /conservation-audit is registered twice in repos/activity-api/src/routes/activities.ts. That route does not exist there. The real duplicate was a different path. Because nothing verified the premise, that one mislocalized gap spawned a family of 31 gaps, 30 still open, and burned 12 compose attempts, every one of them trying to anchor on code that is not in the file. A deterministic check at spec-build time would have stopped the whole family.

WHY THE CHECK TESTS THE QUOTED FORM. A bare substring test gives false negatives: this file contains the string conservation-audit inside a URL and inside a different route named conservation-audit-emit. Only the quoted form, the path wrapped in single or double quotes, distinguishes a real route registration from an incidental mention.

Replace this line, which occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file (this is your verbatim anchor):
          const anchorLabel = startLine > 0 ? "Anchor (verbatim near edit site)" : "Anchor (verbatim top of file)";

with exactly these five lines:
          const premiseTokens = Array.from(new Set(String(summary).split(" ").filter((w) => w.startsWith("/")).map((w) => w.split(",")[0] ?? "").map((w) => w.split(")")[0] ?? "").filter((w) => w.length > 5)));
          const missingPremise = premiseTokens.filter((t) => !liveLines.some((l) => l.includes("'" + t + "'") || l.includes('"' + t + '"')));
          if (missingPremise.length > 0) { console.warn("[gap-to-feature] PREMISE UNVERIFIED: gap names " + missingPremise.join(", ") + " but no quoted occurrence exists in " + firstTarget); }
          const premiseWarning = missingPremise.length > 0 ? (" — PREMISE WARNING: this gap names " + missingPremise.join(", ") + " but NO quoted occurrence of it exists anywhere in this file, so the gap is probably MISLOCALIZED. Do NOT invent an anchor for it. If you cannot identify the real target in the excerpt below, emit ZERO ops and report the false premise instead.") : "";
          const anchorLabel = startLine > 0 ? ("Anchor (verbatim near edit site)" + premiseWarning) : ("Anchor (verbatim top of file)" + premiseWarning);

SCOPE NOTES. summary, liveLines, firstTarget and startLine are all already in scope here; summary is a string. anchorLabel is interpolated into the spec a few lines below, so appending the warning to it is what carries the message to the drafter, which is the point: a log line alone has no reader.

CONSTRAINTS. Exactly one edit op on that one line. No helper function, no imports, no other line changed. Must typecheck with no new errors.

